WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.550
LINKDO. It's got backlinks. It's what bots craaave. (A spoof of Brawndo, from the film Idiocracy.)

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:11.950
Why do bots crave Linkdo? 'Cause it's got backlinks. What's a backlink? It's what they make Linkdo out of. The reasoning runs in a circle.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:19.950
Our pages link to our pages. Kin vouchin' for kin: that's nepotism. The bots swarm it.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:27.550
One week on motdang.net, 20–26 Sept 2026: 1,016,102 bot visits came in off our own links. 882 pages opened by people.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:35.950
So what do bots crave? Water. Like from the toilet? No. Like from the well. Somethin' new, and somethin' they can check.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:44.350
A glass of water: somethin' you saw, counted or asked, with the date. A source a stranger can open, on somebody else's site. From outside the loop: bots fed on bots forget the rare stuff first.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.950
What Bots Craaave. The whole 'splainer, with sources: nanobotco.github.io/bots-crave
